      "writtenOn": "2018-06-14T18:46:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this would be a little easier to read if the early return was seperated and put first.\nI.e \n\nif (desired_state \u003d\u003d led_state || desired_state \u003d\u003d LED_NUM_STATES || period \u003d\u003d LED_INDEFINTE)\n  /* Nothing todo */\n  return;\n\nled_state \u003d desired_state;\n....",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "95094472d7db793ba26c61bef1d94229b31b5272",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a0588a4_bd3a4fe7",
        "filename": "baseboard/octopus/led_states.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-14T19:05:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it would be more readable with the return cases first.  I don\u0027t think desired_state \u003d\u003d led_state can return though because we may need to blink the LED.  \n\nShould the LED_NUM_STATES case return or proceed with the previous state\u0027s LED behavior?  Yorp\u0027s function had it returning without altering the LED, but I noticed coral\u0027s has that scenario continue using the old led_state\u0027s behavior (so blinking if the previous state blinked, I assume).  I suppose we could also make a default state for the LED to resort to as well, if that would be a better route.",
      "parentUuid": "33a8b1b5_1ff92c46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "95094472d7db793ba26c61bef1d94229b31b5272",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46a0103a_98dd790f",
        "filename": "baseboard/octopus/led_states.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-14T19:17:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yeah, you are right (desired_state \u003d\u003d led_state \u0026\u0026 period \u003d\u003d LED_INDEFINITE) seems like the right early return\n\nIf desired_state is invalid, then I like the idea of staying on the previous state and continuing to service that (e.g. blink if we need too)",
      "parentUuid": "4a0588a4_bd3a4fe7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 9
      },
